facts.value:
The routine bios executes a TRAP #13 exception. The parameters
passed depend on the particular BIOS function in each case.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns -1 when there are characters waiting in
the buffer, and 0 if this is not the case.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns the status of the output device, namely -1
if characters could be written, and 0 if the buffer is full.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns a bit-vector for the connected (mounted)
drives.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns 0 if the access was successful, otherwise
a negative number.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns the previous (or current) value of the
vector.
<br>&nbsp;

The BIOS routine Tickcal returns the number of milliseconds
that have elapsed between two calls of the system timer.
<br>&nbsp;
<br><b>Note:</b> For this the function accesses the <a href="/historical/en/the-system-variables/#UDO__timr_ms">_timr_ms</a> system
variable.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns 0x4253494D ('BSIM') if <a href="/historical/en/bsim-bios-extension/#BSIM">BSIM</a> is
available.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns 0 in DO on success, or -1 if there is no
disk in memory.
<br>&nbsp;

The BIOS routine save_disk saves data from memory to the
disk.
<br>&nbsp;

The function only returns a defined result, namely the blink
rate, if the number 5 or 7 was passed in the parameter <i>func</i>.
<br>&nbsp;

All TOS versions.
<br>Parameters 6 and 7 are available with TOS version &gt;= 1.02.
<br>&nbsp;

»Get look up table registers« - Reads several entries from
the colour table into a specified buffer.
<br>&nbsp;

»Get current shift mode value« - Reads the shift mode
register (the current mode of the video shifter).
<br>&nbsp;

The XBIOS routine EgetShift reads out the shift mode register
and returns the contents of the register.
<br>&nbsp;

»Set color look up bank« - Sets the bank for the colour table
from the 16 available.
<br>&nbsp;

»Set color entry« - Writes an entry into the colour table for
an individual colour.
<br>&nbsp;

»Set/clear gray mode« - Switches on or off the colour
interpretation in the video shifter.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns the previous value of the video shifter's
grey bit.
<br>&nbsp;

The function is available only in the TOS of the Atari TT
(when the high word of the '_VDO' cookie has the value of 2).
<br>&nbsp;

»Set palette registers« - Sets several entries in the colour
table from the specified buffer.
<br>&nbsp;

»Set shift mode register« - Sets the shift mode registers of
the video shifter.
<br>&nbsp;

»Set/clear video smear mode« - Switches on (1) or off (0) the
smear mode of the video shifter.
<br>&nbsp;

The XBIOS routine Getrez obtains the current resolution of the
screen.
<br>&nbsp;

»logical screen RAM base« - Returns a pointer to the logical
start address of the video memory.
<br>&nbsp;

The XBIOS routine Logbase obtains the logical start address of
the RAM region currently being used for the video memory.
<br>&nbsp;

The function returns the start address of the logical screen
memory.
<br>&nbsp;

The function is only available on computers of the Falcon
series.
<br>&nbsp;

»physical screen ram base« - Returns the physical start
address of the video memory.
<br>&nbsp;

The XBIOS routine Physbase returns the physical start address
of the RAM region currently being used for the video memory.
<br>&nbsp;

The function Physbase returns the start address of the physical
screen memory.
<br>&nbsp;

This XBIOS routine corresponds to the <a href="/historical/en/setscreen/">Setscreen</a> function with
additional parameters, and serves for altering the screen resolution
and screen memory addresses.
<br>&nbsp;
<a id="MI_MAGIC"></a>
<br><br>
<div><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Historical table"><table class="historical-table prm-rule-table">
<tbody><tr>
  <td>Parameter</td>
  <td>Meaning</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td>par1</td>
  <td>Depending on function - see below</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td>par2</td>
  <td>Depending on function - see below</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td>rez</td>
  <td>always 0x4D49 (MI_MAGIC)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
  <td>command</td>
  <td>Command</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table></div>
</div>

<br>The following values are defined for <i>command</i>:
<br>&nbsp;
<dl>
<dd><a id="CMD_GETMODE"></a></dd>
<dt><b>CMD_GETMODE (0)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Getting current mode
<br>&nbsp;
<br>int32_t mode;
<br>Setscreen(-1, &amp;mode, MI_MAGIC, CMD_GETMODE);
<br>&nbsp;
</p></dd><dd><a id="CMD_SETMODE"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_SETMODE (1)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Set new graphic mode
<br>&nbsp;
<br>int32_t mode=0x1023 /* 800*608*16 */
<br>Setscreen(-1, mode, MI_MAGIC, CMD_SETMODE)
<br>&nbsp;
<br><a href="/historical/en/bios/">BIOS</a> and <a href="/historical/en/vdi/">VDI</a> will be initialised. Not the <a href="/historical/en/aes/">AES</a>.
<br>&nbsp;
</p></dd><dd><a id="CMD_GETINFO"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_GETINFO (2)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Get screen info structure for mode
<br>&nbsp;
</p><pre><a href="/historical/en/screeninfo/">SCREENINFO</a> si;
/* Structure size has to be set         */
si.size=sizeof(<a href="/historical/en/screeninfo/">SCREENINFO</a>);
/* ID of the mode or 0 for current mode */
si.devID=0x1023;
/* status of the operation              */
si.scrFlags=0;
<a href="/historical/en/setscreen/">Setscreen</a>(-1, &amp;si, MI_MAGIC, CMD_GETINFO);
if(si.scrFlags &amp; <a href="/historical/en/screeninfo/#SCRINFO_OK">SCRINFO_OK</a>)
  puts("OK");
else
  puts("Error");
</pre>
</dd><dd><a id="CMD_ALLOCPAGE"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_ALLOCPAGE (3)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Allocate 2nd screenpage
<br>&nbsp;
</p><pre>int32_t adr=0;      /* Frame address or -1 */
<a href="/historical/en/setscreen/">Setscreen</a>(&amp;adr, mode, MI_MAGIC, CMD_ALLOCPAGE);
if(adr)
  puts("OK");
else
  puts("Error");
</pre>
<br>This only allocates one page. A further call will only return
the frame address.
<br>&nbsp;
</dd><dd><a id="CMD_FREEPAGE"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_FREEPAGE (4)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Release 2nd screenpage
<br>&nbsp;
<br>Setscreen(-1, -1, MI_MAGIC, CMD_FREEPAGE)
<br>&nbsp;
<br>The graphics card memory will be released again. If the second
page had still been active the call will switch back to the first page
with <a href="/historical/en/logbase/">Logbase</a> and <a href="/historical/en/physbase/">Physbase</a> set.
<br>&nbsp;
</p></dd><dd><a id="CMD_FLIPPAGE"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_FLIPPAGE (5)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Switch to 2nd screenpage
<br>&nbsp;
<br>Setscreen(-1, -1, MI_MAGIC, CMD_FLIPPAGE)
<br>&nbsp;
<br>Will switch to the second screenpage. <a href="/historical/en/logbase/">Logbase</a> and <a href="/historical/en/physbase/">Physbase</a> will
be set.
<br>&nbsp;
</p></dd><dd><a id="CMD_ALLOCMEM"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_ALLOCMEM (6)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Allocate memory on the graphics card
<br>&nbsp;
</p><pre><a href="/historical/en/scrmemblk/">SCRMEMBLK</a> blk;

blk.size=sizeof(<a href="/historical/en/scrmemblk/">SCRMEMBLK</a>);
/* alloc a block of 200 lines*/
blk.blk_y=200;

<a href="/historical/en/setscreen/">Setscreen</a>(-1, &amp;blk, MI_MAGIC, CMD_ALLOCMEM);
if(blk.blk_start)
  puts("OK");
else
  puts("Out of memory");
</pre>
<br>The width of the block is currently always the width of the
virtual screen. For the hardware functions this block will be like a
screen (0,0,blk_w,blk_h), the coordinates start in the top left corner
(0,0). It will be internally recalculated.
<br>&nbsp;
</dd><dd><a id="CMD_FREEMEM"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_FREEMEM (7)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Release graphics card memory
<br>&nbsp;
<br>Setscreen(-1, &amp;blk, MI_MAGIC, CMD_FREEMEM)
<br>blk of the block to be released.
<br>&nbsp;
</p></dd><dd><a id="CMD_SETADR"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_SETADR (8)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Set screen to fixed address
<br>&nbsp;
</p><pre>/* logical address or -1  */
int32_t logbase=blk.blk_start;
/* physical address or -1 */
int32_t physbase=blk.blk_start;

<a href="/historical/en/setscreen/">Setscreen</a>(logbase, physbase, MI_MAGIC, CMD_SETADR);
</pre>
</dd><dd><a id="CMD_ENUMMODES"></a></dd>
<dd><a id="ENUMMODE_EXIT"></a></dd>
<dd><a id="ENUMMODE_CONT"></a></dd>
<p></p>


<dt><b>CMD_ENUMMODES (9)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> Requests all available modes, since 13.01.2000
<br>&nbsp;
</p><pre>int32_t cdecl enumfunc(<a href="/historical/en/screeninfo/">SCREENINFO</a> *inf,int32_t flag)
{
  printf("%s\n",inf-&gt;name);
  return ENUMMODE_CONT;
}

<a href="/historical/en/setscreen/">Setscreen</a>(-1, &amp;enumfunc, MI_MAGIC, CMD_ENUMMODES);
</pre>
<br>The function "enumfunc" will be called once for every
available mode. ENUMMODE_EXIT (0) will cancel CMD_ENUMMODES.
ENUMMODE_CONT (1) will continue. The parameters are handed over to the
stack using the C standard.
<br>&nbsp;
<p></p>

</dd>
<dt><b><a href="/historical/en/setscreen-ct60/#CMD_TESTMODE">CMD_TESTMODE</a> (10)</b></dt>
<dd>
<p> This function only exist inside the ct60 with internal <a href="/historical/en/tos/">TOS</a>
Radeon driver.
<br>&nbsp;
</p>

</dd>
</dl>

